  "findings": [
    {
      "challengedBy": [],
      "claim": "The new deleteMany OR clause removes any workflow reminder whose retryCount is greater than 1, but the handler increments retryCount on every failed scheduling attempt. That means a reminder is deleted on the third run, after just two failures, instead of being retained until a higher retry threshold or handled explicitly. The changed deleteMany cleanup adds retryCount as a standalone OR branch, so the retry cleanup can delete WorkflowReminder rows for other method values instead of keeping the SMS method scope.",
